@startuml beta-feedback
title Beta Feedback Current Architecture

' Purpose: Show the implemented feedback persistence boundary behind the protected feedback API.

actor "Signed-in Beta User" as BetaTester
participant "App UI or Caller" as AppUi
participant "Feedback API Route" as FeedbackApi
participant "Auth.js Session Read" as AuthJs
participant "Beta Access Policy" as BetaPolicy
participant "Admin Access Policy" as AdminPolicy
participant "Feedback Repository" as FeedbackRepo
participant "Drizzle ORM" as Drizzle
database "Postgres" as Postgres

BetaTester -> AppUi: Trigger feedback submission flow if exposed
AppUi -> FeedbackApi: POST result context and optional note
FeedbackApi -> AuthJs: Read signed-in session
FeedbackApi -> BetaPolicy: Check invited beta access

alt Invited beta identity
  BetaPolicy --> FeedbackApi: Allow feedback write
  FeedbackApi -> FeedbackRepo: Build approved feedback record
  FeedbackRepo -> Drizzle: Insert feedback row
  Drizzle -> Postgres: feedback table
  FeedbackApi --> AppUi: 201 Created
else Missing session or non-invited identity
  BetaPolicy --> FeedbackApi: 401/403
  FeedbackApi --> AppUi: Feedback not saved
end

AppUi -> FeedbackApi: GET feedback records if admin flow is used
FeedbackApi -> AuthJs: Read signed-in session
FeedbackApi -> AdminPolicy: Check admin access

alt Admin identity
  AdminPolicy --> FeedbackApi: Allow feedback read
  FeedbackApi -> FeedbackRepo: Load feedback records
  FeedbackRepo -> Drizzle: Select feedback rows
  Drizzle -> Postgres: feedback table
  FeedbackApi --> AppUi: 200 OK with feedback records
else Non-admin identity
  AdminPolicy --> FeedbackApi: 401/403
  FeedbackApi --> AppUi: Feedback records not returned
end

note right of FeedbackRepo
Implemented persistence foundation:
user id, email, result context, timestamp,
and optional note.
No feedback review UI is implemented in this slice.
end note

@enduml